+#     adjacency -- it is a STAND-IN for the phrase boundary, and it merges a character's file with its
+#     neighbouring nominal run ('maya' + 'championship'), which is what flipped the inferred-emotion arm.
+#
+# THE BRAIN.  One perceived object, one object file (Kahneman, Treisman & Gibbs 1992).  One noun phrase, one
+# discourse referent (Karttunen 1976's discourse referent; Heim 1982's file card): the card is opened by a
+# DETERMINER PHRASE, not by a noun, and the determiner is read ON the card (Heim's Novelty-Familiarity
+# Condition).  The phrase's head is its RIGHTMOST member in English (Williams 1981's Right-Hand Head Rule),
+# so a content noun that lies inside a later noun's phrase is a MEMBER of that phrase, not a referent of its
+# own.  WHERE the mention was said is part of the card (recency and distance are cues on it).
+#
+# THE BOUNDARY IS THE READER'S OWN PARSE, not a chunker: the phrase is the head plus its PRE-HEAD dependents
+# (`hdlab/attachment_arm.py` through `hdlab.frontend.parser`), intersected with the categories that can be
+# NP-internal material (the category organ), and CLOSED at the determiner -- the D is the phrase's outermost
+# layer (Abney 1991), so a second determiner opens a second phrase.  POST-head dependents are NOT absorbed
+# (the prior `boundary_nphead` finding).  `mode`:
+#     "cat"    -- the category run alone (arc-free; what pri 134's chunk did)
+#     "arc"    -- the arc projection alone
+#     "both"   -- the conjunction (DEFAULT, selected on GUM TRAIN)
+#     "graded" -- "both", with the attachment arm's GRADED head belief deciding the uncertain token
+#                 (MAP membership: P(this token's head is inside the phrase) >= P(outside); no threshold
+#                 is fitted -- 0.5 IS the MAP boundary)
+# ===============================================================================================================
+RPN_SPAN = os.environ.get("HDLAB_RPN_SPAN", "1") == "1"
+RPN_BOUNDARY = os.environ.get("HDLAB_RPN_BOUNDARY", "both")
+RPN_COLLAPSE = os.environ.get("HDLAB_RPN_COLLAPSE", "1") == "1"
