+# The categories a determiner phrase can contain to the LEFT of its head.  A VERB / AUX / ADP / SCONJ /
+# CCONJ / PUNCT closes the phrase -- the same domain boundary `coref._np_domain` and the attachment arm's
+# NP_SPLIT cue already use, so a phrase can never cross its clause's verb.
+_NP_LEFT = frozenset(("DET", "ADJ", "NUM", "NOUN", "PROPN", "PART", "PRON", "SYM", "X", "ADV"))
+_NP_LEFT_MAX = 8
+_POSS_DET = frozenset({"my", "your", "his", "her", "its", "our", "their", "whose"})
+# absorbing one of these CLOSES the phrase on its left: the determiner is the DP's outermost layer, so the
+# next token to the left belongs to a different phrase ('the dog the cat saw' is two phrases, not one).
+_CLOSES_LEFT = frozenset(("DET",))
